@coalition_menu
on-arrival: {!
Q.psi_majority = 0;
Q.in_coalition = 0;
Q.in_unstable_coalition = 0;
Q.centre_left_coalition = 0;
Q.left_wing_coalition = 0;
Q.socialist_catholic_coalition = 0;
Q.grand_coalition = 0;
Q.centre_right_coalition = 0;
Q.anti_socialist_coalition = 0;

Q.liberal_aid_accepted = 0;
Q.liberal_budget_accepted = 0;
Q.liberal_crackdown_accepted = 0;
Q.liberal_foreign_accepted = 0;
Q.liberal_nationalisation_accepted = 0;
Q.liberal_reform_accepted = 0;

Q.catholic_charity_accepted = 0;
Q.catholic_education_accepted = 0;
Q.catholic_nationalisation_accepted = 0;
Q.catholic_papacy_accepted = 0;
Q.catholic_women_accepted = 0;
!}

- @pnf_majority
- @psi_majority
- @left_wing_coalition
- @centre_left_coalition
- @socialist_catholic_coalition
- @grand_coalition
- @centre_right_coalition
- @anti_socialist_coalition

@pnf_majority
title: PNF majority alone
subtitle: PNF: [+ pnf_seating_disp +]%
view-if: pnf_seating_disp >= 50 and prime_minister != "D'Annunzio"
on-arrival: {!
Q.prime_minister_party = "PNF";
Q.prime_minister = Q.pnf_leader;
!}

Our worst fears have come true. The PNF have managed to gain a majority in the elections, and secure a two-thirds majority in the Chamber of Deputies.

What now?

- @civil_war: We cannot wait any longer. Mobilise the Red Guard!
- @nothing: Bide our time further.

@nothing
subtitle: This will end the game.

[+ pnf_leader +] acts fast, as the Red Guard is harassed and attacked by both government and right-wing paramilitaries. In the Chamber of Deputies, the assassination of Giacomo Matteotti by government forces sparks momentary outrage while [+ pnf_leader +] seizes the opportunity and quickly consolidates <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> into one-party dictatorship.

<span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.

@psi_majority
title: [+ psi_name +] majority alone
subtitle: [+ psi_name +]: [+ psi_seating_disp +]%
view-if: psi_seating_disp >= 50
on-arrival: {!

if (Q.reformists_defect == 0 && Q.reformist_strength > Q.communist_strength && Q.reformist_strength > Q.maximalist_strength || Q.communist_split == 1 && Q.maximalists_resign == 1) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Turati"; 
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
}

if (Q.communist_split == 0 && Q.communist_strength > Q.reformist_strength && Q.communist_strength > Q.maximalist_strength || Q.reformists_defect == 1 && Q.maximalists_resign == 1) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Bordiga"; 
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
}

if (Q.maximalists_resign == 0 && Q.maximalist_strength > Q.communist_strength && Q.maximalist_strength > Q.reformist_strength || Q.communist_split == 1 && Q.reformists_defect == 1) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Serrati"; 
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
}

if (Q.reformists_defect == 1 && Q.communist_split == 1 && Q.maximalists_resign == 1) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Bacci";
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
    Q.workers_psi -= 4*(1-Q.dissent);
    Q.middle_class_psi -= 5*(1-Q.dissent);
}

Q.psi_in_government = 1; 
Q.psi_majority = 1; 

Q.foreign_minister_party = Q.psi_name; 
Q.foreign_minister = "Matteotti";
Q.interior_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
Q.interior_minister = "Turati"; 
Q.justice_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
Q.justice_minister = "Treves";
Q.labour_minister_party = Q.psi_name; 
Q.labour_minister = "Rigola";
Q.finance_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
Q.finance_minister = "Lazzari";
Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
Q.treasury_minister = "Modigliani";
Q.agriculture_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
Q.agriculture_minister = "Graziadei"; 
Q.public_education_minister_party = Q.psi_name; 
Q.public_education_minister = "Togliatti";
Q.public_works_minister_party = Q.psi_name;
Q.public_works_minister = "Vella";
!}
achievement: governo_monocolore

Finally, the [+ psi_name +] can govern alone! Our long campaign of electioneering has paid off. We do not need to worry about coalition government; anything is possible. 

[+ prime_minister +] is elected within the party to become Prime Minister.

@left_wing_coalition
title: Can we form a Left-Wing Coalition?
subtitle: [+ psi_name +] [? if psri_relation >= psri_min_relations :+ PSRI ?] [? if pri_allies :+ PRI?] [? if psu_coalitioning :+ PSU?] [? if ds_allies :+ [+ ds_name +]?] [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ left_wing_coalition_r +]%) [? if left_wing_coalition_r < 50: Dissident Republicans, Socialists [? if pri_prominent = 0:& the Italian Republican Party?] are willing to provide toleration to the coalition. ?]
view-if: left_wing_coalition_r >= left_wing_minimum
choose-if: (participating = 1 or maximalist_participating = 1) and psri_relation >= psri_min_relations and left_wing_coalition_failed = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ psi_name +] + PSRI [? if pri_allies :+ PRI?] [? if psu_coalitioning :+ PSU?] [? if ds_allies :+ [+ ds_name +]?] [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ left_wing_coalition_r +]%). [? if not_participating = 1: The party has already decided against parliamentary means. ?][? if psri_relation < psri_min_relations : Our relations with the PSRI are too poor. ?][? if left_wing_coalition_failed : Our coalition partners refuse to form another government so soon after the previous one failed. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.leverage = Q.leverage * 1.5;
Q.psi_in_government = 1;
Q.psri_in_government = 1;
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.left_wing_coalition = 1;

if (Q.pri_allies == 1) {
    Q.pri_in_government = 1;
}

if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
    Q.ds_in_government = 1;
}

if (Q.psu_coalitioning == 1) {
    Q.psu_in_government = 1;
}

Q.foreign_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
if (Q.psu_coalitioning == 1) {
    Q.interior_minister_party = "PSU";
} else {
    Q.interior_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
}
Q.justice_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
Q.labour_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
Q.finance_minister_party = "PSRI";
if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
} else {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
}
Q.treasury_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
if (Q.pri_allies == 1) {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = "PRI"; 
} else {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
}
Q.public_works_minister_party = "PSRI";
!}
achievement: sinistra_ascendente

Our negotiations with our coalition allies goes smoothly, and we form a stable coalition.

Who should we select to be Prime Minister?

- @turati
- @bissolati
- @bonomi

@centre_left_coalition
title: Open negotiations with the UL and LDR.
subtitle: [+ psi_name +] + PSRI + [+ ldr_name +] [? if pri_allies :+ PRI?] [? if ds_allies :+ [+ ds_name +]?] [? if ul_allies:+ [+ ul_name +]?] [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ centre_left_coalition_r +]%). [? if (((centre_left_coalition_r + ul_seating_disp) >= 50) and (centre_left_coalition_r <= 50)) and not ul_allies : We will have to negotiate with the [+ ul_name +] to secure a majority coalition. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: [+ psi_name +] + PSRI + [+ ldr_name +] [? if pri_allies :+ PRI?] [? if ds_allies :+ [+ ds_name +]?] [? if ul_allies:+ [+ ul_name +]?] [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ centre_left_coalition_r +]%). [? if not_participating = 1 : The party has already decided against parliamentary means. ?][? if maximalist_participating = 1 : The party has decided against coalitions with any bourgeois parties. ?][? if ldr_relation < ldr_min_relations : We do not have adequate relations with the [+ ldr_name +]. ?][? if ldr_negotiations_failed : The liberals are unwilling to enter into talks again. ?][? if southern_land_reformed = 1 : The [+ ldr_name +] has vowed against coalitions with us since our southern land reforms. ?][? if centre_left_coalition_failed : Our coalition partners refuse to form another government so soon after the previous one failed. ?]
view-if: centre_left_coalition_r >= 50
choose-if: participating = 1 and ldr_relation >= ldr_min_relations and ldr_negotiations_failed = 0 and southern_land_reformed = 0 and centre_left_coalition_failed = 0
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.centre_left_coalition_r >= 50) {
    Q.psi_in_government = 1;
    Q.psri_in_government = 1;
    Q.ldr_in_government = 1;

    if (Q.pri_allies == 1) {
        Q.pri_in_government = 1;
    }

    if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
        Q.ds_in_government = 1;
    }

    if (Q.ul_allies == 1) {
        Q.ul_in_government = 1;
    }

    Q.centre_left_coalition = 1;
    Q.in_coalition = 1;
    Q.in_unstable_coalition = 1;

    Q.foreign_minister_party = Q.ldr_name; 
    if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
        Q.interior_minister_party = Q.ds_name;
    } else {
        Q.interior_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
    }
    Q.justice_minister_party = Q.ldr_name;
    if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
        Q.labour_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
    } else {
        Q.labour_minister_party = Q.ldr_name;
    }
    Q.finance_minister_party = "UL";
    if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
        Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
    } else {
        Q.treasury_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
    }
    Q.agriculture_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
    if (Q.pri_allies == 1) {
        Q.public_education_minister_party = "PRI"; 
    } else {
        Q.public_education_minister_party = Q.ldr_name; 
    }
    if (Q.ul_allies == 1) {
        Q.public_works_minister_party = Q.ul_name; 
    } else {
        Q.public_works_minister_party = "PSRI";
    }
}
!}
on-departure: liberal_negotiations = 0;
go-to: liberal_demands

@socialist_catholic_coalition 
title: Open negotiations with the PPI.
subtitle: [+ psi_name +] + PSRI + PPI [? if pri_allies :+ PRI?] [? if ds_allies :+ [+ ds_name +] ?] [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ socialist_catholic_coalition_r +]%).
unavailable-subtitle: [+ psi_name +] + PSRI + PPI [? if pri_allies :+ PRI?] [? if ds_allies :+ [+ ds_name +] ?] [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ socialist_catholic_coalition_r +]%). [? if not_participating = 1 : The party has already decided against parliamentary means. ?][? if maximalist_participating = 1 : The party has decided against coalitions with any bourgeois parties. ?][? if ppi_relation < ppi_min_relations : We do not have adequate relations with the PPI. ?][? if ppi_negotiations_failed = 1 : We have already tried negotiating with the Catholics. ?][? if catholic_coalition_failed : The Catholics are unwilling to accept another coalition right after the previous one failed. ?][? if secularised_education = 1 : The PPI has vowed against coalitions with us since our education reforms. ?][? if papal_relation < 5 : Our relations with the Holy See are too poor. ?][? if socialist_catholic_coalition_failed : Our coalition partners refuse to form another government so soon after the previous one failed. ?]
view-if: socialist_catholic_coalition_r >= 50 and catholic_coalition_failed = 0
choose-if: participating = 1 and ppi_relation >= ppi_min_relations and ppi_negotiations_failed = 0 and secularised_education = 0 and socialist_catholic_coalition_failed = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.psi_in_government = 1;
Q.psri_in_government = 1;
Q.ppi_in_government = 1;

if (Q.pri_allies == 1) {
    Q.pri_in_government = 1;
}

if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
    Q.ds_in_government = 1;
}

Q.socialist_catholic_coalition = 1;
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.in_unstable_coalition = 1;

Q.foreign_minister_party = "PPI"; 
if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
    Q.interior_minister_party = Q.ds_name;
} else {
    Q.interior_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
}
Q.justice_minister_party = "PPI";
if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
    Q.labour_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
} else {
    Q.labour_minister_party = "PSRI";
}
Q.finance_minister_party = "PPI";
if (Q.ds_allies == 1) {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
} else {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
}
Q.treasury_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
if (Q.pri_allies == 1) {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = "PRI"; 
} else {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = "PSRI"; 
}
Q.public_works_minister_party = "PPI";
!}
on-departure: catholic_negotiations = 0
go-to: catholic_demands

@grand_coalition
title: [? if (socialist_catholic_coalition_r >= 50) or (centre_left_coalition_r >= 50) : Refuse to form a government, and let the other parties assume responsibility. ?][? if (socialist_catholic_coalition_r < 50) and (centre_left_coalition_r < 50) : We are unable to form a government. The task is handed over to the Liberals. ?]
view-if: centre_right_coalition_r < 50 and anti_socialist_coalition_r < 50
subtitle: PSRI + PPI + [+ ldr_name +] + [+ ul_name +] + [+ ds_name +] + Others [? if pll_formed :+ PLL?]: ([+ grand_coalition_r +]%). 
go-to: grand_coalition_yes if (socialist_catholic_coalition_r < 50) or (centre_left_coalition_r < 50 and ul_allies) or ((centre_left_coalition_r + ul_seating_disp < 50) and (not ul_allies)) or not_participating = 1

Are we sure we wish to give up our opportunity to form the government?

- @grand_coalition_yes: Yes, we will abdicate our responsibility for government formation, and let a coalition without us take power.
- @coalition_menu: Actually, we wish to form a coalition after all.

@centre_right_coalition
title: Centre-Right Coalition
subtitle: PNF + [+ ul_name +] [? if ds_enemies:+ [+ ds_name +]?] [? if ldr_enemies:+ [+ ldr_name +]?] [? if pcs_formed :+ PCS ?]: ([+ centre_right_coalition_r +]%)..
on-arrival: {!
Q.centre_right_coalition = 1;
Q.pnf_in_government = 1;
Q.ul_in_government = 1;

if (Q.ds_enemies == 1) {
    Q.ds_in_government = 1;
}

if (Q.ldr_enemies == 1) {
    Q.ldr_in_government = 1;
}

Q.prime_minister = Q.ul_leader;

Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ul_name;

Q.foreign_minister_party = Q.ul_name; 
if (Q.ds_enemies == 1) {
    Q.interior_minister_party = Q.ds_name;
} else {
    Q.interior_minister_party = "PNF"; 
}
Q.justice_minister_party = Q.ul_name;
if (Q.ds_enemies == 1) {
    Q.labour_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
} else {
    Q.labour_minister_party = "UL";
}
Q.finance_minister_party = "PNF";
if (Q.ldr_enemies == 1) {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ldr_name; 
} else {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ul_name; 
}
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "PNF"; 
if (Q.ldr_enemies == 1) {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = Q.ldr_name; 
} else {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = "PNF"; 
}
Q.public_works_minister_party = "PNF";
!}
view-if: centre_right_coalition_r >= 50 and ul_seating_disp + ldr_seating_disp >= pnf_seating_disp 

@anti_socialist_coalition
title: Anti-Socialist Coalition
subtitle: PNF + [+ ul_name +] [? if ds_enemies:+ [+ ds_name +]?] [? if ldr_enemies:+ [+ ldr_name +]?]  [? if pcs_formed :+ PCS ?]: ([+ anti_socialist_coalition_r +]%).
on-arrival: {!
Q.anti_socialist_coalition = 1;
Q.pnf_in_government = 1;
Q.ul_in_government = 1;

if (Q.ds_enemies == 1) {
    Q.ds_in_government = 1;
}

if (Q.ldr_enemies == 1) {
    Q.ldr_in_government = 1;
}

if (Q.pnf_leader == "Grand Council") {
    Q.prime_minister = "Balbo";
    Q.pnf_leader == "Balbo";
} else {
    Q.prime_minister = Q.pnf_leader;
}

Q.prime_minister_party = Q.pnf_name;

Q.foreign_minister_party = Q.ul_name; 
if (Q.ds_enemies == 1) {
    Q.interior_minister_party = Q.ds_name;
} else {
    Q.interior_minister_party = "PNF"; 
}
Q.justice_minister_party = Q.ul_name;
if (Q.ds_enemies == 1) {
    Q.labour_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
} else {
    Q.labour_minister_party = "UL";
}
Q.finance_minister_party = "PNF";
if (Q.ldr_enemies == 1) {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ldr_name; 
} else {
    Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ul_name; 
}
Q.treasury_minister_party = Q.ul_name; 
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "PNF"; 
if (Q.ldr_enemies == 1) {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = Q.ldr_name; 
} else {
    Q.public_education_minister_party = "PNF"; 
}
Q.public_works_minister_party = "PNF";
!}
view-if: anti_socialist_coalition_r >= 50 and pnf_seating_disp > ul_seating_disp + ldr_seating_disp and (prime_minister_party != "PNF" or prime_minister = "D'Annunzio")
go-to: dannunzio_power if prime_minister = "D'Annunzio"

It seems our <span style="color: [+ communist_colour +];">radicalism</span> and abstentionism has pushed the LDR and UL to ally with the PNF, as a junior partner to their list. [+ pnf_leader +] has made himself crucial to this coalition, and been able to come out on top in the inter-party struggle, being appointed Prime Minister by the <span style="color: [+ i_colour +];">**King**</span>.

- @pnf_prime_minister: What now?

@dannunzio_power

The PNF, under the leadership of Gabriele D'Annunzio, is able to form a coalition, keeping himself as Prime Minister in a majority coalition.

What now?

- @civil_war: We cannot wait any longer. Mobilise the Red Guard!
- @nothing_dannunzio: Bide our time further.

@nothing_dannunzio
subtitle: This will end the game.

[+ pnf_leader +] acts fast, consolidating <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> into a corporative state and empowering the PNF and D'Annunzio into effective dictators of <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> for the foresseable future.

<span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.

@grand_coalition_yes
subtitle: [? if participating = 1 : This is extremely unpopular with the Reformist faction. ?]
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.participating == 1) {
    Q.reformist_dissent += 15;
}
Q.psi_in_government = 0; 
if (Q.year == 1919) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Nitti"; 
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ldr_name;
} 
if (Q.year == 1920 || Q.year == 1921) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Giolitti";
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ul_name;
}
if (Q.year == 1921) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Bonomi";
    Q.prime_minister_party = "PSRI";
}
if (Q.year > 1921) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Orlando";
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ldr_name;
}
Q.interior_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
Q.foreign_minister_party = "UL"; 
Q.justice_minister_party = "I"; 
Q.treasury_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.finance_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.public_works_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
Q.public_education_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.labour_minister_party = "UL";
!}

Though tense negotiations between the <span style="color: [+ ldr_colour +];">Liberals</span> and newly formed <span style="color: [+ ppi_colour +];">Catholic</span> parties, the coalition of the PPI, [+ ldr_name +], [+ ul_name +] and [+ ds_name +] is established.

@turati
title: Filippo Turati for Prime Minister
subtitle: Turati leads the Reformist wing, and is an acceptable candidate for Prime Minister.
choose-if: reformists_defect = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Turati is no longer a member of the [+ psi_name +].
on-arrival: psi_in_government = 1; prime_minister = "Turati"; prime_minister_party = psi_name;
go-to: ministries

Filippo Turati's appointment as Prime Minister is approved by all our potential allies.

@bissolati
title: Leonida Bissolati for Prime Minister
view-if: not bissolati_dead
subtitle: Bissolati is a prominent leader of the PSRI, formerly affiliated with the [+ psi_name +].
on-arrival: psi_in_government = 1; prime_minister = "Bissolati"; prime_minister_party = "PSRI"; leverage += 5; maximalist_dissent += 2; communist_dissent += 5;
go-to: ministries

This is highly unexpected, but Bissolati's PSRI roots, as well as his commitment to <span style="color: #9B0000;">socialism</span>, leaves little grumbling from our party.

@bonomi
title: Ivanoe Bonomi for Prime Minister
view-if: bissolati_dead
subtitle: Bonomi is a prominent leader of the PSRI, formerly affiliated with the [+ psi_name +].
on-arrival: psi_in_government = 1; prime_minister = "Bonomi"; prime_minister_party = "PSRI"; leverage += 5; maximalist_dissent += 4; communist_dissent += 7;
go-to: ministries

This is highly unexpected, but Bonomi's PSRI roots leaves merely some grumbling from our party.

@orlando
title: Let the [+ ldr_name +] have their Prime Minister. This will improve our leverage.
subtitle: Vittorio Emanuele Orlando will be reappointed Prime Minister. This is unexpected and will cause internal dissent, but may give us a better position in negotiating for other cabinet positions.
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; maximalist_dissent += 5; communist_dissent += 10; ldr_relation += 10; ds_relation += 5; prime_minister = "Orlando"; prime_minister_party = ldr_name; psi_in_government = 1; leverage += 10
go-to: ministries

@giolitti
title: Let the [+ ul_name +] have their Prime Minister. This will improve our leverage.
subtitle: Giovanni Giolitti will be reappointed Prime Minister. Allowing Giolitti to become Prime Minister is unexpected, and controversial within the party.
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 7; maximalist_dissent += 9; communist_dissent += 12; ldr_relation += 5; ul_relation += 10; prime_minister = "Giolitti"; prime_minister_party = ul_name; psi_in_government = 1; leverage += 10
go-to: ministries

This is highly unexpected, and many in the centre and even the Reformist faction of our party is criticizing this decision.

@gasperi
title: Let the PPI have their Prime Minister. This will improve over leverage.
subtitle: Alcide De Gasperi will be appointed Prime Minister. This is unexpected and will cause internal dissent, but may give us a better position in negotiating for other cabinet positions.
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; maximalist_dissent += 5; communist_dissent += 10; ppi_relation += 10; prime_minister = "De Gasperi"; prime_minister_party = "PPI"; psi_in_government = 1; leverage += 5
go-to: ministries

This is highly unexpected, and many in the centre and even the Reformist faction of our party is criticizing this decision.

@liberal_demands
go-to: l_demands_menu

Having met with representatives from the [+ ldr_name +], they have put forward a series of demands we are to either complete or policies we cannot change while in power.
While it seems do have a bit of wiggle room to negotiate, we certainly cannot outright refuse them. What do we do?

**We will have one year to complete the crackdown of violence if given to us.**

Some major ones include: Land Reform, Streetfighting Crackdowns, and Nationalisations,

While some minor ones are: Budget Surplus, Foreign Affairs and Soviet Aid.

@l_demands_menu

- #libdem_major
- #libdem_minor
- @refuse_libdem
- @finalise_libdem
- #drop_libdem_major
- #drop_libdem_minor

@liberal_reform
title: End our violent seizure of land in the South and reject any form of land reform.
subtitle: This will be a major setback if we are to solve the Southern Question anytime soon.
tags: libdem_major
view-if: liberal_reform_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_reform_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 20;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a major point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us significant progress in negotiations.

@liberal_crackdown
title: Begin a crack down of violence in the streets, including the Red Guard.
subtitle: This will force us to rely on the loyalties of government forces.
tags: libdem_major
view-if: liberal_crackdown_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_crackdown_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 20; liberal_crackdown_timer = 12;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a major point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us significant progress in negotiations.

@liberal_nationalisation
title: Reject any form of nationalisation to the Italian economy.
subtitle: This will limit our ability to reform the current economic system.
tags: libdem_major
view-if: liberal_nationalisation_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_nationalisation_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 20;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a major point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us significant progress in negotiations.

@liberal_budget
title: Maintain a budget surplus.
subtitle: This will limit our ability to conduct government policy. [? if budget < 0 : We will be inheriting a deficit, so we will have to implement temporary austerity. ?]
tags: libdem_minor
view-if: liberal_budget_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_budget_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 10;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a minor point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us some progress in negotiations.

@liberal_foreign
title: Maintain our current alignment with the Entente.
subtitle: This will hamper our actions if we are to control the Foreign Ministry.
tags: libdem_minor
view-if: liberal_foreign_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_foreign_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 10;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a minor point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us some progress in negotiations.

@liberal_aid
title: Reject any form of aid to the Soviet Union.
subtitle: This will limit our ability to improve relations with the Soviet Union.
tags: libdem_minor
view-if: liberal_aid_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_aid_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 10;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a minor point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us some progress in negotiations.

@drop_liberal_reform
title: Drop our promise to reject land reform.
tags: drop_libdem_major
view-if: liberal_reform_accepted = 1
on-arrival: liberal_reform_accepted = 0; liberal_negotiations -= 20;
go-to: l_demands_menu

@drop_liberal_crackdown
title: Drop our promise to crack down on street violence.
tags: drop_libdem_major
view-if: liberal_crackdown_accepted = 1
on-arrival: liberal_crackdown_accepted = 0; liberal_negotiations -= 20; liberal_crackdown_timer = 0;
go-to: l_demands_menu

@drop_liberal_nationalisation
title: Drop our promise to reject nationalisation.
tags: drop_libdem_major
view-if: liberal_nationalisation_accepted = 1
on-arrival: liberal_nationalisation_accepted = 0; liberal_negotiations -= 20;
go-to: l_demands_menu

@drop_liberal_budget
title: Drop our promise to maintain a surplus.
tags: drop_libdem_minor
view-if: liberal_budget_accepted = 1
on-arrival: liberal_budget_accepted = 0; liberal_negotiations -= 10;
go-to: liberal_demands

@drop_liberal_foreign
title: Drop our promise to keep alignment with the Entente.
tags: drop_libdem_minor
view-if: liberal_foreign_accepted = 1
on-arrival: liberal_foreign_accepted = 0; liberal_negotiations -= 10;
go-to: l_demands_menu

@drop_liberal_aid
title: Drop our promise to reject aid to the Soviet Union.
tags: drop_libdem_minor
view-if: liberal_aid_accepted = 1
on-arrival: liberal_aid_accepted = 0; liberal_negotiations -= 10;
go-to: l_demands_menu

@refuse_libdem
title: It seems we cannot come to an agreement.
subtitle: Maybe one with the Catholics might work?
on-departure: ldr_negotiations_failed = 1
go-to: coalition_menu 

@finalise_libdem
title: It seems we have come to an agreement.
subtitle: This is an unstable coalition, to say the least.
choose-if: liberal_negotiations >= ldr_negotiations_min
unavailable-subtitle: The Liberals are not satisfied with the current arrangement.
on-departure: catholic_coalition_failed = 0; 

With the coalition agreed upon, it is time to choose a Prime Minister.

- @turati
- @orlando
- @giolitti 
- @bonomi
- @bissolati

@catholic_demands
go-to: c_demands_menu

Having met with representatives from the PPI, they have put forward a series of demands we are to either complete or policies we cannot change while in power.
While it seems do have a bit of wiggle room to negotiate, we certainly cannot outright refuse them. What do we do?

**We will have one year to complete the Roman Question if demanded to us.**

Some major ones include the Roman Question, Catholic Schools and Family Structure.

While some minor ones are Charity, Nationalisations and the Prime Minister.

@c_demands_menu

- #catholic_major
- #catholic_minor
- @refuse_catholic
- @finalise_catholic
- #drop_catholic_major
- #drop_catholic_minor

@catholic_papacy
title: Resolve the Roman Question with the Papacy.
subtitle: This will benefit our <span style="color: [+ ppi_colour +];">Catholic</span> bloc as well if we can form a compromise in time.
tags: catholic_major
view-if: catholic_papacy_accepted = 0 and roman_question_answered = 0
on-arrival: catholic_papacy_accepted = 1; catholic_negotiations += 20; catholic_papacy_timer = 12;
go-to: c_demands_menu

This is a major point of conjecture for the PPI, and secures us significant progress in negotiations.

@catholic_education
title: Reject any changes to <span style="color: [+ ppi_colour +];">Catholic</span> schools.
subtitle: This will limit our abilities to secularise education.
tags: catholic_major
view-if: catholic_education_accepted = 0
on-arrival: catholic_education_accepted = 1; catholic_negotiations += 20;
go-to: c_demands_menu

This is a major point of conjecture for the PPI, and secures us significant progress in negotiations.

@catholic_women
title: Reject any changes to the traditional family structure and women's rights.
subtitle: This will limit our ability to institute reforms to laws as divorce or marriage.
tags: catholic_major
view-if: catholic_women_accepted = 0
on-arrival: catholic_women_accepted = 1; catholic_negotiations += 20;
go-to: c_demands_menu

