@finalise_catholic
title: It seems we have come to an agreement.
subtitle: This is an unstable coalition, to say the least.
choose-if: catholic_negotiations >= ppi_negotiations_min
unavailable-subtitle: The Catholics are not satisfied with the current arrangement.
on-departure: socialist_catholic_coalition = 1; liberal_coalition_failed = 0;
go-to: chooseable_pm if not catholic_pm_accepted; nonchooseable_pm if catholic_pm_accepted

@chooseable_pm

With the coalition agreed upon, it is time to choose a Prime Minister.

- @turati
- @gasperi

@nonchooseable_pm

With the coalition agreed upon, we should make do on our promises.

- @gasperi

@ministries

We can pick from any number of ministries. Controlling a ministry allows us to directly effect policy in that area.

- #mins_1919
- #drop_mins_1919

@labour
title: Labour and Social Security Ministry
subtitle: Taking the Labour Ministry is expected of us.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1919
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: labour_minister_party != psi_name
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; labour_minister_party = psi_name; labour_minister = "Rigola"
go-to: ministries

Rinaldo Rigola of the [+ psi_name +] has been appointed Labour and Social Security minister.

@interior
title: Interior Ministry
subtitle: The Interior Ministry controls domestic security.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1919
choose-if: leverage >= 10
view-if: interior_minister_party != psi_name
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; interior_minister_party = psi_name; interior_minister = "Turati" if not reformists_defect; interior_minister = "Bacci" if reformists_defect;
go-to: ministries

[? if not reformists_defect : Filippo Turati of the [+ psi_name +] has been appointed Interior Minister. ?]

[? if reformists_defect : Giovanni Bacci of the [+ psi_name +] has been appointed Interior Minister. ?]

